It's a major balance issue for the game.

Certain classes are allowed skill in crossbow rather than bow, but there 
are no bolt traps to loot for ammo.

The best class ammowise has got to be the Ranger because they start with 
scores of arrows, ought to score more arrows than they lose by looting 
and each arrow is very light and scores resonable damage.  And if that 
isn't enough arrows for you then go complete your quest.

Rocks are heavy and glass tends to break too easily to make slings 
worthwhile.  Darts also break and do piddling damage unless posioned or 
a lot of enchantment is wasted on them when they break.  (Unlike with 
arrows you can't even reuse the launcher's to-hit bonus.)

Crossbow bolts do little damage, don't even come in silver and are 
fairly rare outside the mines.

Daggers are heavy and do little damage, but there are supposed to be 
some silver daggers out there somewhere and daggers last almost forever 
so it's worth max-enchanting your primary quiver of daggers with full 
protection, especially for those classes that are skilled or better with 
dagger.  Unlike bows or crossbows, daggers don't hog a hand and they 
last much longer than darts while doing more damage.

Sure the ye old 2.5d30 Rogue rain of death is going away real soon now, 
but daggers will still be a good skill investment and worth carrying around.

